## 10. What a green pipeline proves — say it plainly

- [ ] You can state, in one sentence, what a green run of your promotion
      pipeline actually establishes.
- [ ] You can state what it does **not** establish — in particular, whether any
      automated end-to-end test drives the built artifact against the live
      environment, and whether any core user flow (login, the primary feature,
      billing) is exercised by CI at all.

> **"It deployed successfully" and "it was proven to work" are different
> claims.** Reporting the former as the latter is the failure this section
> exists to prevent — in a status update, in a release note, and in an agent's
> summary of its own work.

---

## Explicitly unsolved — do not record these as design decisions

1. **Schema-drift detection between deployed environments.** There is none.
   Resetting a fresh *local* database from migration files is not a
   cross-environment diff. The one real drift ever found here was found by a
   human doing manual inspection.
2. **Cross-environment secret-value parity checking.** There is none. See § 7.

Their absence is a gap, not a considered choice. Do not copy it forward as one.

